---
import TopicLayout from '../../layouts/TopicLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/");
---
<TopicLayout
  title="Barolo"
  subtitle="Red Wine · Piedmont, Italy"
  parentLabel="Wine Types"
  parentPath={`${base}wine-types/`}
  description="A comprehensive guide to Barolo — the king of Italian wines. The Nebbiolo grape, the communes, the great producers, and how to read the label."
  stats={[
    { value: '100% Nebbiolo', label: 'Grape' },
    { value: '~2,000 ha', label: 'Vineyard area' },
    { value: 'DOCG 1980', label: 'Classification' },
    { value: 'Min. 3 years', label: 'Aging (Barolo)' },
    { value: 'Min. 5 years', label: 'Aging (Riserva)' },
    { value: '10–30+ years', label: 'Peak' },
  ]}
  toc={[
    { id: 'overview',    label: 'Overview' },
    { id: 'region',      label: 'The Region' },
    { id: 'nebbiolo',    label: 'The Grape: Nebbiolo' },
    { id: 'terroir',     label: 'Terroir & The Two Soils' },
    { id: 'production',  label: 'Production & Styles' },
    { id: 'mga',         label: 'The Great Vineyards (MGA)' },
    { id: 'label',       label: 'Reading the Label' },
    { id: 'producers',   label: 'Notable Producers' },
    { id: 'price',       label: 'Price Guide' },
    { id: 'pairing',     label: 'Food Pairing' },
  ]}
>

  <!-- OVERVIEW -->
  <section id="overview" class="topic-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Overview</h2>
    <p class="section-lead">
      Barolo is Italy's most profound and age-worthy red wine — produced from 100% Nebbiolo in the Langhe hills of Piedmont. It is known as <em>il re dei vini, il vino dei re</em> — the king of wines, the wine of kings. High in tannin, high in acid, and pale in colour, it is a wine that requires patience: young Barolo can be forbiddingly austere. Given a decade, it becomes one of the most complex and compelling wines in the world.
    </p>
    <div class="section-body">
      <p>Like Burgundy, Barolo's logic is terroir-driven: the commune, the vineyard, the vintage, and the producer all matter. Two Barolos from adjacent vineyards can taste radically different. Two from the same vineyard but different producers can be equally so.</p>
      <p>DOCG status since 1980. 100% Nebbiolo, from 11 permitted communes. Minimum 38 months aging (18 in oak). Riserva: minimum 62 months (24 in oak).</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE REGION -->
  <section id="region" class="topic-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">The Region</h2>
    <p class="section-lead">The Barolo DOCG zone covers approximately 2,000 hectares in the Langhe hills of Piedmont, roughly 70 km south of Turin. The landscape is one of rolling hills, medieval hilltop villages, and south- to southwest-facing amphitheatres of vines.</p>

    <!-- SVG Map -->
    <div class="map-container">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 380 340" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="region-map" aria-label="Map of the Barolo DOCG communes">

        <!-- Soil zone backgrounds -->
        <!-- Tortonian zone (west/northwest) -->
